[56.583336, "o", "\r\u001b[2KThe default `python3` (3.13.1 in `/usr/local`) has a `pip` launcher script but the `pip` package itself is missing. I'll inspect the interpreter's paths and the\r\nalternate system Python, and test package installation.\r\n\r\n```\r\necho '--- /usr/local python sys ---'; /usr/local/bin/python3 -c 'import sys, site; print(sys.executable); print(sys.version); print(\"prefix\",sys.prefix); \r\nprint(\"base_prefix\",sys.base_prefix); print(\"path:\"); [print(p) for p in sys.path]; print(\"site-packages\", site.getsitepackages()); print(\"user\", \r\nsite.getusersitepackages())' 2>&1; echo '--- /usr/bin python ---'; /usr/bin/python3 --version 2>&1; /usr/bin/python3 -c 'import sys; print(sys.executable); \r\n[print(p) for p in sys.path]' 2>&1; /usr/bin/pip3 --version 2>&1; echo '--- pip launcher ---'; head -20 /usr/local/bin/pip 2>&1; ls -la /usr/local/bin/pip* \r\n/usr/local/lib/python3.13/site-packages 2>&1 | head -100\r\n```\r\n\u001b[32m⠹\u001b[0m Waiting for the LM to respond..."]
[56.583835, "o", "\r\u001b[2K\u001b[32m⠹\u001b[0m Waiting for the LM to respond...\r\n\u001b[?25h\r\u001b[1A\u001b[2K"]
