[60.673132, "o", "\r\u001b[2KThe `/usr/local` Python 3.13 site-packages contains only `pip-24.3.1.dist-info`; the actual `pip` module was removed. I'll verify whether the bundled \r\n`ensurepip` wheel is available so pip can be restored offline.\r\n\r\n```\r\necho '--- ensurepip ---'; /usr/local/bin/python3 -m ensurepip --version 2>&1; /usr/local/bin/python3 -c 'import ensurepip, os; print(ensurepip.__file__); \r\np=os.path.join(os.path.dirname(ensurepip.__file__), \"_bundled\"); print(p); print(os.listdir(p))' 2>&1; echo '--- dist-info files ---'; find \r\n/usr/local/lib/python3.13/site-packages/pip-24.3.1.dist-info -maxdepth 2 -type f -printf '%P\\n' | sort | head -50; echo '--- pip cache ---'; find \r\n/root/.cache/pip -maxdepth 4 -type f 2>/dev/null | head -20\r\n```\r\n\u001b[32m⠇\u001b[0m Waiting for the LM to respond..."]
