[64.071, "o", "\r\u001b[2KThe bundled pip 24.3.1 wheel is present, so the cleanest repair is to run the interpreter's own `ensurepip` to reinstall pip into the system Python. Then I'll \r\ntest `pip --version` and an actual package installation.\r\n\r\n```\r\n/usr/local/bin/python3 -m ensurepip --upgrade --default-pip 2>&1; echo '--- verify import/version ---'; /usr/local/bin/python3 -m pip --version 2>&1; \r\n/usr/local/bin/pip --version 2>&1; /usr/local/bin/python3 -c 'import pip; print(pip.__version__, pip.__file__)' 2>&1\r\n```\r\n\u001b[32m⠋\u001b[0m Waiting for the LM to respond..."]
[64.071314, "o", "\r\u001b[2K\u001b[32m⠋\u001b[0m Waiting for the LM to respond...\r\n\u001b[?25h\r\u001b[1A\u001b[2K"]
