[68.842151, "o", "\r\u001b[2K`ensurepip` incorrectly treats the orphaned `.dist-info` metadata as a satisfied installation and skips reinstalling the missing files. I'll move that stale \r\nmetadata aside, rerun `ensurepip`, and verify the module is restored.\r\n\r\n```\r\nset -e\r\nBK=/tmp/pip-dist-info-backup-$(date +%s)\r\nmkdir -p \"$BK\"\r\nmv /usr/local/lib/python3.13/site-packages/pip-24.3.1.dist-info \"$BK\"/\r\necho \"backed up to $BK\"\r\n/usr/local/bin/python3 -m ensurepip --upgrade --default-pip 2>&1\r\necho '--- verify ---'\r\n/usr/local/bin/python3 -m pip --version\r\n/usr/local/bin/pip --version\r\n/usr/local/bin/python3 -c 'import pip; print(pip.__version__, pip.__file__)'\r\n```\r\n\u001b[32m⠏\u001b[0m Waiting for the LM to respond..."]
[68.842471, "o", "\r\u001b[2K\u001b[32m⠏\u001b[0m Waiting for the LM to respond...\r\n\u001b[?25h\r\u001b[1A\u001b[2K"]
