[86.386995, "o", "\r\u001b[2K\r\n\u001b[1;31mmini-swe-agent\u001b[0m\u001b[31m (step \u001b[0m\u001b[1;31m7\u001b[0m\u001b[31m, \u001b[0m\u001b[1;31m$0.00\u001b[0m\u001b[31m):\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[32m⠦\u001b[0m Waiting for the LM to respond..."]
[86.387651, "o", "\r\u001b[2KThe end-to-end index install succeeded. To verify the actual system-wide path (not just `--target`), I'll install a small package into the real site-packages, \r\nimport it with the system interpreter, run `pip check`, and clean up temporary test artifacts.\r\n\r\n```\r\nset -e\r\n/usr/local/bin/python3 -m pip install --no-cache-dir --disable-pip-version-check six 2>&1\r\n/usr/local/bin/python3 -c 'import six; print(\"system import:\", six.__version__, six.__file__)'\r\n/usr/local/bin/python3 -m pip check 2>&1\r\n/usr/local/bin/python3 -m pip show pip 2>&1 | sed -n '1,12p'\r\nrm -rf /tmp/pip-install-test\r\necho '--- sanity across entrypoints ---'\r\n/usr/local/bin/python3 -m pip --version\r\n/usr/local/bin/pip3.13 --version\r\n/usr/bin/pip3 --version\r\n```\r\n\u001b[32m⠦\u001b[0m Waiting for the LM to respond..."]
[86.388019, "o", "\r\u001b[2K\u001b[32m⠦\u001b[0m Waiting for the LM to respond...\r\n\u001b[?25h\r\u001b[1A\u001b[2K"]
[87.603594, "o", "\r\n\u001b[1;32mTool\u001b[0m:\r\n"]
